<title>HONG KONG: Consortium signs HK airport maintenance franchise.</title>
<headline>Consortium signs HK airport maintenance franchise.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>China Aircraft Services Ltd said on Thursday it had signed a franchise agreement with the Hong Kong Airport Authority for the provision of aircraft maintenance services at the new airport from its opening in April 1998.</p>
<p>The Hong Kong-based company is a joint venture held 40 percent by China National Aviation Corp, and 20 percent by each of British Airways Plc, Hutchison Whampoa Ltd's Hutchison Whampoa (China) Ltd, and UAL Corp's United Airlines Inc.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
